Production builds on QA data (3 holdings, about 20 months of history), median of 7 runs. Before: `80657fb9` (#341). After: this branch.

| What | Before | After | Change |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Open a holding on Accounts, desktop / mobile | not possible | 67 / 57 ms | new |
| Open portfolio value on Accounts, desktop / mobile | not possible | 54 / 52 ms | new |
| Open Wealth drawer, desktop / mobile | 81 / 85 ms | 126 / 119 ms | +45 / +34 ms: it now also loads and draws the value history; under the 50 ms threshold |
| Open Accounts, desktop / mobile: LCP | 128 / 136 ms | 152 / 128 ms | +24 / −8 ms (noise threshold 50 ms; one extra parallel query for holdings) |
| Open Wealth, desktop / mobile: LCP | 464 / 440 ms | 456 / 440 ms | same |
| Open Home, desktop / mobile: LCP | 476 / 472 ms | 480 / 456 ms | same |
| JS: Accounts / Wealth | 171 / 166 KB | 171 / 167 KB | within budget (183 / 186 KB) |

The first version opened a holding in 360 ms: `next/dynamic` made React hold the reveal for about 300 ms. The component now loads in parallel with the data.

## Checks

- `npm test` (1923 passed), `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck`, `npm run build`, `npm run check:bundle`: passed.
- `e2e/net-worth.gated.spec.ts` and `e2e/service-keys.mocked.spec.ts`: 10 passed against a production build.
- New unit tests: values before the first sync from the shares held then; nothing calculated when trades don't add up; month rows; average buy price, gain and portfolio share.
- Reverse paths unchanged: disconnect removes stored charts and trades (the recorded values stay), reset all data removes everything.
- Not run: `desktop:smoke` (nothing under `desktop/`, no new files read at runtime).

## Decisions

- **Recorded first, calculated before.** From the first sync on, values are what Scalable reported. Earlier values are shares from the stored trades × Scalable's stored prices, marked `*`, and only when those trades add up exactly to the shares held now and never go below zero. Otherwise the view says why and starts at the first sync. No day without a stored price gets a point.
- The value chart spaces points by date, because older prices are further apart.
- A value change includes shares bought or sold; the price % beside it is the market move. The text under the table says so.
- Trade amounts are shares × price without fees or taxes. Trade prices exist once the history job has read the trade's details; otherwise "price not stored".
- Not shown: sold positions (they are no longer holdings), per-holding dividends and fees (not stored per security), crypto coins (Scalable gives one total). 3-month and year-to-date price rows are not stored per security.
- No new chat tool: the assistant already reads quotes and price charts from Scalable.
- Charts reuse `NetWorthChart` and `ScalablePositionChart`.

